WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.969 --> 00:00:04.690
So it seems like we sort of can't just have
a normal weekend.

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:10.930
The latest is that the Demoine register canceled
the release of the last Iowa primary poll

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:13.670
before today's caucus in Iowa.

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:19.560
But in the poll that did come out, Bernie
Sanders has jumped to a 13 point advantage

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:25.349
over Joe Biden with Elizabeth Warren and second
place, seven points behind Bernie.

00:00:25.349 --> 00:00:30.369
So let's take it as, I love to do a step at
a time tonight is the Iowa caucuses.

00:00:30.369 --> 00:00:33.730
These are the first votes in the 2020 democratic
primary.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:34.910
It is not a primary.

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:38.571
So instead of you just, you show up at any
time during the day and you vote and then

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:39.571
you leave.

00:00:39.571 --> 00:00:43.640
The way the caucus works is people gather,
they talk about the candidates, they try to

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:48.410
convince other voters come over and support
my candidate and then they take an initial

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:49.550
vote.

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:57.130
The viability threshold in the Iowa caucuses
is 15% so if you take that initial vote and

00:00:57.130 --> 00:01:04.549
your candidate is below 15% in any precinct,
then you have another round of discussion

00:01:04.549 --> 00:01:10.820
and you select another candidate until everybody
remaining has 15% and then the delegates are

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:12.640
allocated proportionately.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:15.360
That's the gist of the way the caucus system
works.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:20.160
The Des Moines register poll is considered
the gold standard Iowa poll and they announced

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:25.030
over the weekend, we're not releasing the
poll results because at least one person who

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:28.850
was surveyed said one of the candidates was
not mentioned.

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:31.490
When they said of the following candidates,
who do you support?

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:33.340
A candidate was left out.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:37.250
Uh, the Des Moines register said, we don't
have evidence that this happened to more than

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:40.170
one person, but we don't have proof that it
didn't.

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:45.830
And so we are canceling the release of the
poll and many people immediately an understandably

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:50.880
very suspicious that this was done either
because Bernie was crushing the results and

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:54.870
they wanted to suppress it or because Bernie
was the one who wasn't mentioned in the list

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:55.870
of candidates.

00:01:55.870 --> 00:02:00.950
We don't know if that's true, but it is immediately
raising suspicions and the temperature of

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:06.750
this entire thing has just increased dramatically
hours before the caucusing starts tonight.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:09.160
Now, meanwhile, there are other polls.

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:15.970
We have a civics DPR or DFP data for progress
poll and the numbers heavily favor Bernie

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:16.970
Sanders.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:25.510
Bernie 28 Warren, 21 Biden and booed edge
edge tied at 15 in an average of recent Iowa

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:32.590
polls going into today's vote, the numbers
are Bernie leading at 24.7 Biden at 21 booted

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:39.760
judge at 16 and Warren 15 now with these numbers,
remember there is proportional allocation

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:42.340
of delegates with these percentages.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:45.750
You would have Bernie get 10 delegates from
Iowa.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:53.069
You would have Biden get nine Buddha judged
seven Warren six but remember there's a 15%

00:02:53.069 --> 00:02:54.470
viability threshold.

00:02:54.470 --> 00:03:01.629
So there's recently, there's a roughly a quarter
of the vote that right now is with candidates

00:03:01.629 --> 00:03:08.320
that are below 15% that support will be reallocated
to the other candidates before the night is

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:09.320
over.

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:10.930
Meaning anyone still could win.

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:15.800
But the most important takeaway, and I don't
want people to forget this, almost anyone

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:20.500
can come away with the most delegates tonight
or with a plurality of the delegates tonight,

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:25.230
but no one is going to do better than get
some momentum because there's only 41 delegates

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:26.230
tonight.

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:33.019
So if Bernie gets nine and Biden gets 10 or
Bernie gets 11 and Biden gets eight, this

00:03:33.019 --> 00:03:37.260
is almost zero in context of the entire democratic
primary.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:39.100
That's not to say it doesn't matter tonight.

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:43.879
The point is tonight is more about momentum
because getting one more delegate than the

00:03:43.879 --> 00:03:45.460
second place person.

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:49.319
In terms of the math, that doesn't do much
in terms of the headlines.

00:03:49.319 --> 00:03:52.030
In terms of the PR, it does a lot.

